{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01KopTDgVc5UxmR9aGc4eDbZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`ai-engineering/answers/01-005-explain-context-windows-and-their-limitations.md`** — Q5: Explain context windows and their limitations.\n\n**What the note covers:**\n- **Concept** — context window as finite working memory (input + output tokens), not just a spec number\n- **Mechanism** — three reasons limits bite in practice: O(n²) attention/KV-cache cost, lost-in-the-middle accuracy degradation (Liu et al. 2023), and linear API cost + TTFT scaling\n- **Mitigation hierarchy** — RAG first (retrieve 5–15 precise chunks), then sliding-window summarization, prompt compression (LLMLingua), and long-context models (Gemini 1.5 / Claude 3.5) only as a last resort with cost quantified\n- **Verbal script** — first-person, opens with the anti-pattern (\"just use a bigger window\") before explaining why that's wrong\n- **Pitfalls** — conflating context size with model quality, recommending long-context models without cost numbers, forgetting the accuracy cliff in the middle\n- **Cross-links** — Q9 (KV cache), Q44 (lost in the middle), Q36 (handling long documents in production)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":55725,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":327,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b1f22e1-41e0-4121-8359-905dd35a3361","uuid":"a0c751f2-2bf5-4571-a6fd-f22fcd858da9"}
